 | `GET/POST /inventory/purchase-orders/` · `GET /inventory/purchase-orders/<ref>/` | 🔐 `procurement.manage` | Purchase-order drafts and immutable line snapshots |
 | `POST /inventory/purchase-orders/<ref>/submit/` · `ordered/` · `receipts/` | 🔐 `procurement.manage` | PO lifecycle and source-keyed partial/full goods receipts; receipts append `RECEIPT` movements and reject over-receipt |
 | `POST /inventory/purchase-orders/<ref>/approve/` | 🔐 `procurement.approve` | Separate maker-checker approval; requester self-approval is rejected |
+| `POST /inventory/purchase-orders/<ref>/reject/` | 🔐 `procurement.approve` | Body `{reason}` (required). Refuses a SUBMITTED order: it returns to `DRAFT` for its requester to correct and resubmit; the reason is appended to the order notes and audited (`PURCHASE_ORDER_REJECTED`) |
+| `POST /inventory/purchase-orders/<ref>/cancel/` | 🔐 `procurement.manage` | Body `{reason}` (required). Withdraws a `DRAFT`/`SUBMITTED` order to the existing `CANCELLED` status — never deletes; replay is a no-op; approved orders are refused |
+| `GET /inventory/procurement/locations/` · `GET /inventory/procurement/items/` | 🔐 `procurement.manage` | Read-only lookups of ACTIVE delivery locations and stock items (purchase-side fields only) for the purchase-order form; the inventory catalogs above stay `inventory.manage` |
+| `GET /inventory/accounting/purchase-orders/` · `GET .../<ref>/` | 🔐 any of `reports.financial.view`, `expense.approve`, `procurement.approve` | Read-only Accounting hand-off: orders from `SUBMITTED` onwards (never drafts) with lines, totals, `total_paid`/`outstanding_amount`, derived `receipt_progress`/`payment_progress`, goods receipts with `received_value`, payments and evidence URLs. Filters: `status`, `supplier_id`, `search` |
+
+Purchase-order create (`POST /inventory/purchase-orders/`): an `idempotency_key` replays exactly one request — the same payload returns the stored order (`200`, "Existing purchase order returned."), a different payload is refused (`400`, `errors.idempotency_key` names the existing order). Unknown or inactive suppliers/locations are `400` field errors (`supplier_id`, `delivery_location_id`).
 | `GET/POST /users/terminals/` · `PATCH /users/terminals/<id>/` | 🔐 `terminal.manage` | Register, label, list (`active`, `department`, `search`), or deactivate optional workstation metadata; current-user presence is informational, not a session lock. `ip_address` registers the address a front desk desk reaches the API from (one address, or a CIDR network; stored canonically, blank clears) and `desktop_ip_registered_at` records when; `receptionist_desktop_ready` reports whether an active FRONT_DESK row can identify the desk at all (key or address). A non-front-desk row never acts as the Receptionist Desktop. |
 | `POST /users/terminals/<id>/desktop-key/` | 🔐 `terminal.manage` | Rotate a FRONT_DESK workstation's desk key (returned once; the previous key stops working) — the per-browser route, kept alongside the registered address. |
 | `GET /users/directory/` | 🔐 dispatch/profile/shift/`payroll.manage` capability | Minimal active-staff picker projection without account-management data; supports employee-code search for authorized payroll preparers. |
